# Line endings, pinned for every checkout on every machine. Git for Windows checks text out
# with CRLF by default. Git Bash itself shrugs that off (measured on windows-latest), but not
# everything that reads these files does: the copies apply-to-vault.py places in an owner's
# vault would carry CRLF into their git history, a plain Cygwin or WSL bash dies on $'\r',
# and a diff would show every line as changed. The repo already stores LF, so on a Mac
# nothing changes.
* text=auto
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.template  text eol=lf
*.plist     text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.md        text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
